macarthur  criticized truman publicly  said there is no substitute for victory  there wasn't much time after the victory  over  germany and japan for popping champagne  corks and celebrating  uh just as the 50 nations that had  joined in defeating the axis powers were  drafting a charter for the united  nations in san francisco the victorious  alliance between the united states and  the soviet union was falling apart  war alliance between the united states  and britain and the soviet union was  tactical  exclusively there was no other  ideological or sentimental attachment  between the nations and  as  the the war appeared to be won in  europe's spring of 1945 the red army  began  uh  occupying more and more portions of  eastern europe with  the clear intention of establishing a  soviet empire this is exactly what  churchill was worried about in march of  1946 winston churchill gave a speech in  america in which he uttered  a phrase that would live on for a long  time he said that from stetton in the  baltic to trieste in the adriatic an  iron curtain has descended across the  continent so  uh what to do about this expansionist  tendency  short of fighting a war  well what truman arrived at was a  conclusion heavily influenced by the  writings of george cannon an american  diplomat in russia who  believed that soviet expansionism was  actually a result of the insecure  unstable nature of the regime itself  and that  the process of expansion was actually a  way of holding that regime together  and that if expansion was prevented  if it was contained  then the regime induced course would  turn in on itself and collapse  this doctrine came to be known as  containment because it was a way of  fighting the soviet regime by containing  it rather than by defeating it at any  rate a sustained confrontation between  the two  remaining superpowers in the world  that would come to be called the cold  war  the cold war turned hot in 1950 on the  korean peninsula  which had been divided since the end of  the war between communist forces in the  north that were aligned with the soviet  union and democratic forces in the south  that were aligned with the united states  this led to an invasion on june 25th  1950 of some 80 000 north korean troops  that swept into the south very nearly  conquering it  and the truman  invoked the united nations  and the american response was funneled  through the united nations so it was  called a police action rather than  a war  there was no declaration of war the war  went very badly until uh  general douglas macarthur got involved  uh  performed a brilliant amphibious  invasion at incheon which cut off the  north korean troops and  led him quickly to be able to round them  up defeat them and then head north  and he kept going north and finally  approached the chinese border and at  that point a quarter of a million  chinese troop  swept in on macarthur and drove him back  to  into south korea with the battle line  finally stabilizing around the 38th  parallel  at this point  macarthur and truman got deadlocked in a  conflict  because  macarthur thought  the time was right the justification was  there for what he called a whole new war  a war against china against communist  china that would  succeed in overthrowing this unfriendly  hostile noxious communist regime  that had just taken power  and thus  avert  the prospect of  a sino-soviet chinese and soviet  alliance that could come to dominate the  world the time was right to take that on  truman on the other hand  thought this was absolutely the wrong  thing that it would be he called it a  booby trap to uh go into a war in china  and rejected the idea macarthur  criticized truman publicly  in an official letter to the house  minority leader  said there is no substitute for victory  in other words a rejection of the  containment doctrine there is no  predefining the fact though that the  korean war was at best a stalemate it  remains a people divided to this day  uh there is no settlement of the war uh  the war is simply suspended so in some  ways it  illustrates some of the  unsatisfactory aspects of the  containment doctrine and that situation  is yet to be resolved  thank you for watching  we hope you're enjoying our highlight  series and invite you to explore all of  hillsdale college's online courses they  are free and for everyone who loves to  learn

